    "column_header": "Column 4",
    "raw_text": "Great famine. Cultivators fled to Malwa for food. Government called them back and made remissions of rent, and also made advances in the shape of Tuccavee. During this year of great distress the then Government distributed grain free of charge; some portions of the Purgunnahs were not-withstanding desolated. The information is obtained from the old hereditary revenue officers. No record, private or public, is forthcoming.",
